55,3,1,talk,Rin,,"I hate the smell of the bin house, so no to C! I think A is okay if we help each other.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
56,3,1,talk,Midori,,"C is too expensive for some of us, and the maintenance costs are worrying. I'm leaning towards A or B.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
57,3,1,talk,Shunichi,,"B sounds like a recipe for more arguments about whose turn it is and where it fits. A is simpler, though strict.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
58,3,1,talk,May,,A requires us to be up at 7:30 AM. That's brutal. But C is a huge project. I'll go with A over the others.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
59,3,1,talk,Asuka,,B is impossible due to the narrow frontages and ward notices. C is too rigid. A is the only logical choice left.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
60,3,2,talk,Rin,,"@May, we can wake each other up! Let's do A!","{""words"":10,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,2,talk,Midori,,"If we choose A, we should be mindful of those who struggle with the early hours. Maybe we can support each other.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,2,talk,Shunichi,,"A keeps the location fixed, which avoids the frontage issue, and avoids the ""broken latch"" arguments of a structure.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,2,talk,May,,"I still hate the time, but compared to a four-month application process for C, I can handle a few early mornings.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,2,talk,Asuka,,"A is the most equitable in terms of space, provided the rotation of supervision is strictly managed.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,3,talk,Rin,,Yay! Everyone seems to like A!,"{""words"":6,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,3,talk,Midori,,It seems the most balanced option for our current situation.,"{""words"":10,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,3,talk,Shunichi,,"It's the least likely to cause a permanent rift, provided we're flexible with the schedule.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,3,talk,May,,"Fine, A it is. But I'm not doing the first shift!","{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,3,talk,Asuka,,I agree. Option A is the most viable.,"{""words"":8,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
